notes.body:
@johnthacker Thank you for your comments. How about following idea that based on your comments but with a little bit extension (based on MR !10058)?

I plan to:

1. Add following code to 'iana_charsets.h':

```c++

/* macro used for creating iana charset enumeration type and enum_val_t array */
#define mibenum_vals_character_sets_VALUE_STRING_LIST(XXX) \
        XXX(IANA_CS_NONE, 0, "*") \
        XXX(IANA_CS_US_ASCII, 1, "US-ASCII") \
        XXX(IANA_CS_ISO_8859_1, 4, "ISO-8859-1") \
        //... \
        XXX(IANA_CS_TIS_620, 2259, "TIS-620") \
        XXX(IANA_CS_CP50220, 2260, "CP50220"")

/* define iana charset enumeration type */
typedef VALUE_STRING_ENUM(mibenum_vals_character_sets) mibenum_vals_character_sets_t;

/* declare iana charset enum_val_t array (using a new marco in epan/params.h)
 * extern const enum_val_t mibenum_vals_character_sets_ev_array[];
 */
VS_LIST_TO_ENUM_VAL_T_ARRAY_GLOBAL_DCL(mibenum_vals_character_sets_ev_array);
```

2. Remove the old way defining mibenum_vals_character_sets in 'iana_charsets.c' and replayed by following code:

```c
/* define value_string array identical to old mibenum_vals_character_sets */
VALUE_STRING_ARRAY(mibenum_vals_character_sets);
/* unchanged code */
value_string_ext mibenum_vals_character_sets_ext = VALUE_STRING_EXT_INIT(mibenum_vals_character_sets);

/* define iana charset enum_val_t array (using a new marco in epan/params.h)
 * with new name mibenum_vals_character_sets_ev_array (not conflic with the
 * name of the value_string array)
 */
VS_LIST_TO_ENUM_VAL_T_ARRAY_GLOBAL_DEF(mibenum_vals_character_sets, mibenum_vals_character_sets_ev_array);
```

3. Then replace code in mibenum_charset_to_encoding() of iana_charsets.c with enum names of charset:

```c
guint
mibenum_charset_to_encoding (guint charset)
{
    ...
        case 4:
            return ENC_NA|ENC_ISO_8859_1;
    ...
    /* replaced to */
        case IANA_CS_ISO_8859_1;
            return ENC_NA|ENC_ISO_8859_1;
```

4. Finally, packet-xml.c or other dissectors can add iana charset enumeration preference like:

```c
prefs_register_enum_preference(xml_module, "default_encoding", "Default charset ...",  &pref_default_encoding, mibenum_vals_character_sets_ev_array, FALSE);
```

Certainly, pref_default_conding should be converted to wireshark charset encoding with ```mibenum_charset_to_encoding()``` before using.

If you agree with this idea, please help to review and merge the MR !10058 , then I will change the code in this MR.

@johnthacker I have modified the code according to the idea that we discussed. The preference of 'Default encoding' changed to:

![XML_charset_preference](/uploads/3f66e327c9c1d70e7a36ad6a1b383688/XML_charset_preference.png)

Please help review. Thanks!

